            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Baltimore to Trenton?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 1 hour 34 minutes to 2 hours 3 minutes, depending on the service and the number of stops.</p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Baltimore to Trenton?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Acela, which can complete the journey in approximately 1 hour and 34 minutes with direct service.</p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Baltimore to Trenton cost?</h3>
            <p>Ticket prices generally fall between:</p>
            <p><b>$11-$40 for early booking on the Northeast Regional Coach</b></p>
            <p><b>$40-$80 for standard Northeast Regional fares</b></p>
            <p><b>$60-$130 for Northeast Regional Business</b></p>
            <p><b>$100-$200+ for Acela Business</b></p>
            <p><b>$150-$250+ for Acela First or last-minute travel</b></p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Baltimore to Trenton?</h3>
            <p>Yes, most Amtrak Northeast Regional, Acela, and long-distance trains are direct, so there’s no need for transfers.</p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café car, and luggage space. Acela adds premium seating, at-seat meal service (First Class), and priority boarding.</p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 2-2.5 hours, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and allows productive travel time.</p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Baltimore to Trenton in one day?</h3>
            <p>Yes, the route is very suitable for same-day trips, with frequent departures allowing a full day in Trenton.</p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Baltimore do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Baltimore Penn Station, located in downtown Baltimore. Some connections are available from BWI Airport Station.</p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Trenton?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Trenton Transit Center, conveniently located in the city center and easily accessible by NJ Transit, SEPTA, and local buses.</p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class or Acela worth it?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom and a quieter environment. At the same time, Acela provides the fastest journey with premium amenities, making both ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 1.5-2 hour journey.</p>













